# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two-qubit gate {#the-two-qubit-gate}"
msgstr "La puerta de dos qubits {#the-two-qubit-gate}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every bond $(i, j)$ of the lattice gets the same two-qubit gate, made of a Heisenberg entangler followed by random fields:\n"
msgstr "Cada enlace $(i, j)$ de la red recibe la misma puerta de dos qubits, formada por un entrelazador de Heisenberg seguido de campos aleatorios:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"U_{ij} =  e^{iJ(X_iX_j + Y_iY_j + Z_iZ_j)}\\; e^{i(h_i Z_i + h_j Z_j)}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"U_{ij} =  e^{iJ(X_iX_j + Y_iY_j + Z_iZ_j)}\\; e^{i(h_i Z_i + h_j Z_j)}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "with $h$ drawn uniformly from $[-\\pi/2, \\pi/2]$ for every gate.\n"
msgstr "con $h$ extraído uniformemente de $[-\\pi/2, \\pi/2]$ para cada puerta.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "> **Question.** How would you decompose $U_{ij}$ into gates the hardware can run?\n"
msgstr "> **Pregunta.** ¿Cómo descompondrías $U_{ij}$ en puertas que el hardware pueda ejecutar?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Answer\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Respuesta\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The fields** are easy. $e^{ihZ}$ is a single-qubit rotation $R_Z(-2h)$ on each qubit.\n"
msgstr "**Los campos** son fáciles. $e^{ihZ}$ es una rotación de un solo qubit $R_Z(-2h)$ en cada qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The entangler** is the hard part. $XX$, $YY$ and $ZZ$ commute, so it factors into three rotations, $R_{XX}$, $R_{YY}$ and $R_{ZZ}$. Each takes two CNOTs, which makes six CNOTs per gate.\n"
msgstr "**El entrelazador** es la parte difícil. $XX$, $YY$ y $ZZ$ conmutan, así que se factoriza en tres rotaciones, $R_{XX}$, $R_{YY}$ y $R_{ZZ}$. Cada una necesita dos CNOT, lo que da seis CNOT por puerta.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There is a better way. Any two-qubit gate can be built from at most three CNOTs and single-qubit rotations. The optimal circuit starts from the form $e^{i(aXX + bYY + cZZ)}$, and this entangler already has that form with $a = b = c = J$. So it maps straight onto three CNOTs, and the single-qubit angles are linear in $J$. The experiment code builds the gate this way.\n"
msgstr "Hay una forma mejor. Cualquier puerta de dos qubits se puede construir con como máximo tres CNOT y rotaciones de un solo qubit. El circuito óptimo parte de la forma $e^{i(aXX + bYY + cZZ)}$, y este entrelazador ya tiene esa forma con $a = b = c = J$. Así que se asigna directamente a tres CNOT, y los ángulos de un solo qubit son lineales en $J$. El código del experimento construye la puerta de esta manera.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "On hardware, every two-qubit gate adds noise, so halving the CNOT count matters.\n"
msgstr "En el hardware, cada puerta de dos qubits añade ruido, por lo que reducir a la mitad el número de CNOT importa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""

