# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulate the $4 \\times 4$ lattice {#simulate-the-4-times-4-lattice}"
msgstr "Simula la red de $4 \\times 4$ {#simulate-the-4-times-4-lattice}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the $4 \\times 4$ lattice, you can do both: compute the exact state at every coupling, and sample every circuit with 10,000 shots, as an experiment would. The shots are stored with shape (batches, shots, qubits), the same layout as the randomizations in the hardware data. Here all 10,000 shots form a single batch, so the bootstrap over batches adds no shot noise, and the error bars in the next plot show only the spread between marginal positions.\n"
msgstr "Para la red de $4 \\times 4$, puedes hacer ambas cosas: calcular el estado exacto en cada acoplamiento y muestrear cada circuito con 10.000 shots, como haría un experimento. Los shots se almacenan con la forma (lotes, shots, qubits), la misma disposición que las aleatorizaciones en los datos de hardware. Aquí los 10.000 shots forman un único lote, por lo que el bootstrap sobre lotes no añade ruido de shots, y las barras de error del siguiente gráfico muestran solo la dispersión entre las posiciones marginales.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. What to measure and how to estimate it {#2-what-to-measure-and-how-to-estimate-it}"
msgstr "2. Qué medir y cómo estimarlo {#2-what-to-measure-and-how-to-estimate-it}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The IPR and the collision entropy {#the-ipr-and-the-collision-entropy}"
msgstr "El IPR y la entropía de colisión {#the-ipr-and-the-collision-entropy}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a marginal $A$ of $n_A$ qubits with bitstring distribution $p_A(a)$, the quantity to estimate is the inverse participation ratio (IPR) of the marginal distribution, and from it the collision entropy:\n"
msgstr "Para una marginal $A$ de $n_A$ qubits con distribución de cadenas de bits $p_A(a)$, la cantidad que hay que estimar es la razón de participación inversa (IPR) de la distribución marginal, y a partir de ella la entropía de colisión:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR}_A = \\sum_a p_A(a)^2, \\qquad S_2[A] = -\\log_2 \\mathrm{IPR}_A\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR}_A = \\sum_a p_A(a)^2, \\qquad S_2[A] = -\\log_2 \\mathrm{IPR}_A\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\mathrm{IPR}_A$ is also the probability that two shots agree on the marginal. A product state has $\\mathrm{IPR}_A = 1$, and a random state has $\\mathrm{IPR}_A \\approx 2^{-n_A}$, so $S_2$ climbs from 0 to about $n_A$ bits as the marginal becomes random.\n"
msgstr "$\\mathrm{IPR}_A$ es también la probabilidad de que dos shots coincidan en la marginal. Un estado producto tiene $\\mathrm{IPR}_A = 1$, y un estado aleatorio tiene $\\mathrm{IPR}_A \\approx 2^{-n_A}$, de modo que $S_2$ sube de 0 a aproximadamente $n_A$ bits a medida que la marginal se vuelve aleatoria.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Estimator 1: count pairs of shots {#estimator-1-count-pairs-of-shots}"
msgstr "Estimador 1: contar pares de shots {#estimator-1-count-pairs-of-shots}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "> **Question.** How do you estimate this quantity from your shots?\n"
msgstr "> **Pregunta.** ¿Cómo estimas esta cantidad a partir de tus shots?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The naive estimator computes each $p(a)$ from the shots as $\\hat p(a) = n_a / N$, then sums $\\sum_a \\hat p(a)^2$.\n"
"This estimator is biased.\n"
msgstr ""
"El estimador ingenuo calcula cada $p(a)$ a partir de los shots como $\\hat p(a) = n_a / N$ y luego suma $\\sum_a \\hat p(a)^2$.\n"
"Este estimador está sesgado.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\sum_a n_a^2 / N^2$ counts every shot as agreeing with itself, which pushes the estimate up: on average it gives $\\mathrm{IPR}_A + (1 - \\mathrm{IPR}_A)/N$ instead of $\\mathrm{IPR}_A$. Since $\\mathrm{IPR}_A$ is the probability that two shots agree, count only pairs of *different* shots:\n"
msgstr "$\\sum_a n_a^2 / N^2$ cuenta cada shot como coincidente consigo mismo, lo que eleva la estimación: en promedio da $\\mathrm{IPR}_A + (1 - \\mathrm{IPR}_A)/N$ en lugar de $\\mathrm{IPR}_A$. Dado que $\\mathrm{IPR}_A$ es la probabilidad de que dos shots coincidan, cuenta solo los pares de shots *distintos*:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\widehat{\\mathrm{IPR}}_A = \\frac{\\sum_a n_a (n_a - 1)}{N (N - 1)}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\widehat{\\mathrm{IPR}}_A = \\frac{\\sum_a n_a (n_a - 1)}{N (N - 1)}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is unbiased, and it is what `ipr_from_shots` below computes.\n"
msgstr "Este estimador es insesgado, y es lo que calcula `ipr_from_shots` más abajo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Estimator 2: Parseval expansion {#estimator-2-parseval-expansion}"
msgstr "Estimador 2: expansión de Parseval {#estimator-2-parseval-expansion}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The IPR can also be written through the parities $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ of all nonempty subsets $S$ of the marginal:\n"
msgstr "El IPR también se puede escribir mediante las paridades $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ de todos los subconjuntos no vacíos $S$ de la marginal:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR}_A = 2^{-n_A}\\Bigl(1 + \\sum_{\\emptyset \\neq S \\subseteq A} \\langle Z_S \\rangle^2\\Bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR}_A = 2^{-n_A}\\Bigl(1 + \\sum_{\\emptyset \\neq S \\subseteq A} \\langle Z_S \\rangle^2\\Bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This form matters because error mitigation methods such as PEA work on expectation values, not on probabilities.\n"
"**One qubit:** The outcome probabilities are $p(0) = (1 + \\langle Z \\rangle)/2$ and $p(1) = (1 - \\langle Z \\rangle)/2$, so\n"
msgstr ""
"Esta forma importa porque los métodos de mitigación de errores como PEA trabajan con valores esperados, no con probabilidades.\n"
"**Un qubit:** Las probabilidades de los resultados son $p(0) = (1 + \\langle Z \\rangle)/2$ y $p(1) = (1 - \\langle Z \\rangle)/2$, por lo que\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR} = p(0)^2 + p(1)^2 = \\frac{1 + \\langle Z \\rangle^2}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
"**A $2 \\times 2$ marginal:** With its qubits labeled $a, b, c, d$, the marginal has $2^4 - 1 = 15$ parities: 4 single qubits, 6 pairs, 4 triples, and the whole marginal, so\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR} = p(0)^2 + p(1)^2 = \\frac{1 + \\langle Z \\rangle^2}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
"**Un marginal de $2 \\times 2$:** Con sus qubits etiquetados como $a, b, c, d$, el marginal tiene $2^4 - 1 = 15$ paridades: 4 qubits individuales, 6 pares, 4 tríos y el marginal completo, por lo que\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR} = \\frac{1}{16} \\Bigl(1\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_d \\rangle^2 \\\\\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a Z_b \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 \\\\\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a Z_b Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_b Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 \\\\\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a Z_b Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 \\Bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR} = \\frac{1}{16} \\Bigl(1\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_d \\rangle^2 \\\\\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a Z_b \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 \\\\\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a Z_b Z_c \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_b Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_a Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 + \\langle Z_b Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 \\\\\n"
"&+ \\langle Z_a Z_b Z_c Z_d \\rangle^2 \\Bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

